          "answer": "**Call emergency services now (999 in the UK, 911 in the US, or your local number).** A drooping mouth and a heavy arm on one side that started suddenly are signs of a possible stroke. Do not wait to see if it passes.\n\nThe stroke guidance says any sudden face drooping or arm weakness is treated as a stroke until proven otherwise, and it says to call emergency services immediately. It also says to note the time the symptoms started, or the last time you were known to be well. For you, that is likely the time you went to sleep or when you were last seen normal. Give that time to the emergency call handler. (Source: red-flag-stroke-symptoms)\n\nOur symptom check labelled this \"routine,\" but that label does not fit what you describe. Please treat this as an emergency.\n\nDo not drive yourself. Do not eat or drink while you wait, in case swallowing is affected. If someone is with you, ask them to stay with you.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
